# /etc/ragnar/apcguard/nmc.list -- cards apcguard must ALWAYS analyse. One card per line: ADDRESS [MAC], IPv4 or IPv6.
#
# Declared cards are PINNED: they are never evicted and are not counted against --max-observed-nmcs, so a
# flood of spoofed SNMP sources cannot push them out. Cards that are only LEARNED from a sysDescr answer
# are capped, and once the cap is hit a card first seen afterwards is ignored (APC-012 says so).
# Declaring cards is what makes Class B work when the tap does not see the card's SNMP replies.
#
# The MAC is optional. Declare a MAC only where the tap sees the card's own frames. It lets apcguard tell the
# card's own ICMP rejection of a tunnel packet from one sent by a firewall on its behalf, and it is the only
# thing that allows a later attempt's severity to be lowered for a card seen rejecting tunnels. In a routed
# topology every frame carries the router's MAC: leave the MAC out there.
# If APC-110 appears for a card, its declared MAC does not match what this tap sees: fix it or remove it.
192.0.2.10        02:aa:bb:cc:dd:10   # rack PDU, row A
2001:db8::10      02:aa:bb:cc:dd:10   # the same card's IPv6 address
192.0.2.11                            # a card whose MAC is not declared
